PATCH 524: three stores of a TRUNCATED HOST POINTER into the far-pointer word DGROUP:0x78e.

DGROUP:0x78e pairs with the segment word at 0x790 as a far pointer.  Three sites write its offset:

    dad2: a1 2c ea   mov ax,[0xea2c]     ; the TCB OFFSET word
    dad5: 05 ea 00   add ax,0xea
    dad8: a3 8e 07   mov [0x78e],ax
  (twice -- FUN_0000_dab0 and its sibling), and

    db07: b8 b8 ed   mov ax,0xedb8       ; a NEAR OFFSET constant
    db0a: a3 8e 07   mov [0x78e],ax

`DAT_2000_aa2c` is #defined as a HOST POINTER -- `g_mem + (word[0xea2e]<<4) + word[0xea2c]` -- so
`DAT_2000_aa2c + 0xea` assigned to the 16-bit `DAT_1000_c78e` stored the low 16 bits of a HOST ADDRESS.
The third site had `(undefined1 *)&DAT_2000_adb8`, i.e. the host address of the DGROUP variable that
happens to live at 0xedb8, where the asm loads the near offset 0xedb8 itself.  Both are patch 516's
class: a host-address-derived value in a DGROUP word, different by construction between gcc -m32 and
emcc.

MEASURED: this is AZER2's remaining native<->wasm divergence.  DGROUP:0x78e held 0x132a on native against
0xd71a on wasm from the first mission frame (word[0xea2c] being 0x1240 / 0xd630 there); two ticks after
the fingerprint first differs, at t=373, native spawns an object into slot DGROUP:0xb8e3 through
b1df <- ba33 <- b5e7 and wasm does not -- with the whole DGROUP otherwise identical at t=372.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -36372,7 +36372,12 @@
